      "content": "The setup and calculation are completely correct! ✅\n$$\\text{Mean} = \\frac{\\sum fx}{n} = \\frac{2(22) + 4(26) + 9(30) + 5(34) + 7(38) + 3(42)}{30} = \\frac{1008}{30} = 33,6$$\n\n**Final Answer:** $33,6$ (or $33.6$)\n\n---\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Formula:** $\\text{Mean} = \\frac{\\sum fx}{n}$\n* **What the letters mean:**\n  * $f$: **Frequency** (how many times each temperature range occurs)\n  * $x$: **Midpoint** (the estimated middle value of each temperature interval)\n  * $\\sum fx$: **Sum of products** (multiplying each frequency by its midpoint, then adding them all together)\n  * $n$: **Total frequency** (the total number of observations, i.e., total days)\n* **Why we use it:** Since exact raw data is lost in grouped intervals, we use the midpoint as a representative value for each group. The mnemonic **FMT** (**F**requency $\\times$ **M**idpoint **T**otal) helps you remember to multiply $f$ by $x$ before adding them up!\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always check if your total frequency ($n$) matches the sum of the frequency column. In this case, $2 + 4 + 9 + 5 + 7 + 3 = 30$, which matches our denominator!"
